sReal` skips unless `ARD_GITLEAKS_BIN` is set, so it did not run here.\n\n## Open issues\n- `PinnedGitleaksVersion` (8.28.0) is my choice. A maintainer should confirm or change it, and run the integration test with a real binary.\n- Shipping the binary in the image needs Dockerfile or deploy/ changes, which are protected paths and are not touched.\n- `.ard/config.yaml` is not edited, so the pass stays off until a maintainer enables it.\n- A maintainer should confirm that #20 is complete.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013BRU8dw1beKjyZNsM7SsxU","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChKx8fF7dAaqvSJyCS8gx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The optional gitleaks pass is in, switched on by a new `redact.gitleaks` config block (off by default). `go test ./...` and `make lint` pass. The real-binary test `TestGitleaksReal` skips unless `ARD_GITLEAKS_BIN` is set, so it did not run here.\n\nThe pass follows the plan: a gitleaks scanner and a helper that chains it after the builtin scan. A hit takes the existing flagged path (log stays host-local, `ard:needs-human`), and a missing binary, error exit, timeout or bad report fails closed. The config path is read per close-out, so enabling it needs no restart.\n\nOpen points, also in `.ard/89/worker-engineer.md`:\n- **Pinned version:** I picked 8.28.0 for `PinnedGitleaksVersion`. A maintainer should confirm it and run the integration test against a real binary.\n- **Image and config:** shipping the binary needs Dockerfile or `deploy/` changes, and enabling the pass needs a change to `.ard/config.yaml`. Both are protected paths, so I left them alone.\n- **#20:** a maintainer should confirm it is complete.\n\nThe Guardrails text in `docs/proposal.md` is updated."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1211,"cache_read_input_tokens":56108,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1211},"output_tokens":409,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e9d6c479-cc3e-4248-8d96-c556a2a58c6d","uuid":"6e561b16-28d1-40ae-b3f0-ddbdbbaef353","timestamp":"2026-11-23T13:38:04.276Z","request_id":"req_011ChKx8f6BjvG3WFGWtbCy9"}
